{
 "fps": 30,
 "lead": 0.8,
 "tail": 2.0,
 "footer": "Sources: canada.ca \u00b7 CRA: determine the province of employment; your province of residence; home office expenses for employees (detailed method, T2200, T777S); instalments; TD1; CRA T4127 (2026) \u00b7 Examples, general info, not advice",
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "L1",
   "file": "vo/L1.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Sam works from his kitchen in Halifax. His company is in Calgary. He has never once set foot in that office."
  },
  {
   "id": "L2",
   "file": "vo/L2.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Every paycheque looked fine. Then he filed his tax return. And he owed four thousand, five hundred and seventy-nine dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L3",
   "file": "vo/L3.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Same salary. Same job. No mistake on his part. Just one box on his T four that nobody explained to him."
  },
  {
   "id": "L4",
   "file": "vo/L4.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And by the end of this video, you'll know which box that is. And the one form that can cut the bill."
  },
  {
   "id": "L5",
   "file": "vo/L5.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Today: what actually happens to your taxes when you work remotely in Canada."
  },
  {
   "id": "L6",
   "file": "vo/L6.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "All numbers: the twenty twenty-six tax year, an eighty-five thousand dollar salary, single, no other income. Examples, not real people. General information, not advice."
  },
  {
   "id": "L7",
   "file": "vo/L7.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "First, the two provinces in Sam's life."
  },
  {
   "id": "L8",
   "file": "vo/L8.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "There's the province where he lives. Nova Scotia."
  },
  {
   "id": "L9",
   "file": "vo/L9.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And there's the province his payroll uses. That's called the province of employment. It's in box ten of his T four."
  },
  {
   "id": "L10",
   "file": "vo/L10.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "These two can be different. And when they are, that's where the trouble starts."
  },
  {
   "id": "L11",
   "file": "vo/L11.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Let's start with the one that decides your tax."
  },
  {
   "id": "L12",
   "file": "vo/L12.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "For the C R A, your provincial tax depends on the province where you lived on December thirty-first."
  },
  {
   "id": "L13",
   "file": "vo/L13.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Not where your employer is. Not where the head office is. Where you live."
  },
  {
   "id": "L14",
   "file": "vo/L14.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Sam lived in Nova Scotia on December thirty-first. So his whole year is taxed at Nova Scotia rates."
  },
  {
   "id": "L15",
   "file": "vo/L15.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, the payroll side."
  },
  {
   "id": "L16",
   "file": "vo/L16.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Your employer has to pick a province for your pay deductions. The C R A has rules for that."
  },
  {
   "id": "L17",
   "file": "vo/L17.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If you report to an office in person, it's the province of that office."
  },
  {
   "id": "L18",
   "file": "vo/L18.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If you don't report to any office, it's generally the province where your employer's business is, and where your pay comes from."
  },
  {
   "id": "L19",
   "file": "vo/L19.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "There's one exception for remote workers. If you'd normally go to a specific office, without your remote work agreement, that office's province can count."
  },
  {
   "id": "L20",
   "file": "vo/L20.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "But Sam was hired remote. There's no office he'd go to. So his employer used Alberta."
  },
  {
   "id": "L21",
   "file": "vo/L21.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And one more detail from the C R A: your home office is generally not your employer's establishment."
  },
  {
   "id": "L22",
   "file": "vo/L22.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "So now we have Sam's whole problem."
  },
  {
   "id": "L23",
   "file": "vo/L23.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "His payroll took tax at Alberta rates. But he owes tax at Nova Scotia rates."
  },
  {
   "id": "L24",
   "file": "vo/L24.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Here's what that looks like in real numbers."
  },
  {
   "id": "L25",
   "file": "vo/L25.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Federal tax is the same everywhere. Only the provincial part changes."
  },
  {
   "id": "L26",
   "file": "vo/L26.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "At Alberta rates, Sam's provincial tax on eighty-five thousand dollars is about four thousand, nine hundred and seventy dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L27",
   "file": "vo/L27.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "At Nova Scotia rates, it's about nine thousand, five hundred and forty-nine."
  },
  {
   "id": "L28",
   "file": "vo/L28.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "His payroll took about fifteen thousand, one hundred and ninety-seven dollars in income tax."
  },
  {
   "id": "L29",
   "file": "vo/L29.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "His real income tax is about nineteen thousand, seven hundred and seventy-six."
  },
  {
   "id": "L30",
   "file": "vo/L30.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "The gap: four thousand, five hundred and seventy-nine dollars. Due with his return."
  },
  {
   "id": "L31",
   "file": "vo/L31.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "That's about one hundred and seventy-six dollars he didn't pay on each paycheque, all year."
  },
  {
   "id": "L32",
   "file": "vo/L32.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, this doesn't always go the wrong way."
  },
  {
   "id": "L33",
   "file": "vo/L33.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Same employer in Alberta, same salary, but a different home."
  },
  {
   "id": "L34",
   "file": "vo/L34.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Live in British Columbia, and Sam would get about five hundred and seventy dollars back."
  },
  {
   "id": "L35",
   "file": "vo/L35.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Live in Ontario, and he'd owe about three hundred and fifty-four."
  },
  {
   "id": "L36",
   "file": "vo/L36.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Manitoba: about two thousand, six hundred and one."
  },
  {
   "id": "L37",
   "file": "vo/L37.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Prince Edward Island: about three thousand, six hundred and seventy-nine."
  },
  {
   "id": "L38",
   "file": "vo/L38.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And Nova Scotia: the four thousand, five hundred and seventy-nine we already saw."
  },
  {
   "id": "L39",
   "file": "vo/L39.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "So the question is never just \"do I work remotely\". It's \"which two provinces are on my paperwork\"."
  },
  {
   "id": "L40",
   "file": "vo/L40.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "But before you blame the payroll department, there's a second half to this story. Because remote work also gives you something."
  },
  {
   "id": "L41",
   "file": "vo/L41.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And this part is worth real money. If you qualify."
  },
  {
   "id": "L42",
   "file": "vo/L42.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "It's the home office deduction. Officially: work space in the home expenses."
  },
  {
   "id": "L43",
   "file": "vo/L43.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Since twenty twenty-three, the temporary flat rate method is gone. There's only one way now: the detailed method."
  },
  {
   "id": "L44",
   "file": "vo/L44.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "To use it, the C R A sets a few conditions."
  },
  {
   "id": "L45",
   "file": "vo/L45.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One. You were required to work from home more than half the time, for at least four weeks in a row."
  },
  {
   "id": "L46",
   "file": "vo/L46.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Two. Your employer signs Form T twenty-two hundred."
  },
  {
   "id": "L47",
   "file": "vo/L47.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Three. Your employer didn't pay you back for those costs."
  },
  {
   "id": "L48",
   "file": "vo/L48.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Sam checks all three. So let's build his claim."
  },
  {
   "id": "L49",
   "file": "vo/L49.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Sam rents. His rent is one thousand, eight hundred dollars a month. Twenty-one thousand, six hundred a year."
  },
  {
   "id": "L50",
   "file": "vo/L50.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Electricity and heat: one thousand, five hundred. His monthly internet fees: nine hundred."
  },
  {
   "id": "L51",
   "file": "vo/L51.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Twenty-four thousand dollars of home costs in total."
  },
  {
   "id": "L52",
   "file": "vo/L52.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Now, what share of that is work?"
  },
  {
   "id": "L53",
   "file": "vo/L53.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Sam's office is a separate room. Ten percent of his apartment's floor space. And he uses it only for work."
  },
  {
   "id": "L54",
   "file": "vo/L54.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "For a room like that, the C R A says you don't count hours. You use the floor space."
  },
  {
   "id": "L55",
   "file": "vo/L55.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Ten percent of twenty-four thousand dollars. A two thousand, four hundred dollar deduction."
  },
  {
   "id": "L56",
   "file": "vo/L56.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "At Sam's tax rate in Nova Scotia, that cuts his tax by about eight hundred and ninety-two dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L57",
   "file": "vo/L57.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "But what if Sam worked at the kitchen table instead?"
  },
  {
   "id": "L58",
   "file": "vo/L58.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Then hours count. The C R A's own example: a space that's twelve percent of the home, used forty hours out of one hundred and sixty-eight in a week."
  },
  {
   "id": "L59",
   "file": "vo/L59.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "That's about two point nine percent."
  },
  {
   "id": "L60",
   "file": "vo/L60.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "On the same twenty-four thousand dollars, that's a six hundred and eighty-six dollar deduction. About two hundred and fifty-five dollars of tax."
  },
  {
   "id": "L61",
   "file": "vo/L61.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Same person. Same job. A separate room is worth more than three times as much."
  },
  {
   "id": "L62",
   "file": "vo/L62.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And some things you can't claim as a salaried employee. Mortgage interest. Property tax. Home insurance. Furniture."
  },
  {
   "id": "L63",
   "file": "vo/L63.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "So where does that leave Sam?"
  },
  {
   "id": "L64",
   "file": "vo/L64.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "He owed four thousand, five hundred and seventy-nine dollars. The home office cuts about eight hundred and ninety-two."
  },
  {
   "id": "L65",
   "file": "vo/L65.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "He still owes about three thousand, six hundred and eighty-seven."
  },
  {
   "id": "L66",
   "file": "vo/L66.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And that number matters for one more reason."
  },
  {
   "id": "L67",
   "file": "vo/L67.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If your net tax owing is more than three thousand dollars this year, and in either of the two years before, the C R A can ask you to pay by instalments."
  },
  {
   "id": "L68",
   "file": "vo/L68.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Four times a year. March, June, September, and December."
  },
  {
   "id": "L69",
   "file": "vo/L69.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "So if Sam does nothing, next year could start with a quarterly bill."
  },
  {
   "id": "L70",
   "file": "vo/L70.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Here's the fix. And it takes five minutes."
  },
  {
   "id": "L71",
   "file": "vo/L71.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "On the federal T D one form, there's a line: additional tax to be deducted."
  },
  {
   "id": "L72",
   "file": "vo/L72.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Sam asks his employer to take about one hundred and forty-two dollars more from each paycheque."
  },
  {
   "id": "L73",
   "file": "vo/L73.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "That spreads the bill across the whole year. No surprise in April."
  },
  {
   "id": "L74",
   "file": "vo/L74.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, the checklist for anyone working remotely."
  },
  {
   "id": "L75",
   "file": "vo/L75.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One. Look at box ten on your T four. That's your province of employment."
  },
  {
   "id": "L76",
   "file": "vo/L76.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Two. Compare it with the province you'll live in on December thirty-first."
  },
  {
   "id": "L77",
   "file": "vo/L77.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Three. If they're different, estimate the gap. Then use the T D one to cover it."
  },
  {
   "id": "L78",
   "file": "vo/L78.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Four. If you were required to work from home, ask your employer for a T twenty-two hundred."
  },
  {
   "id": "L79",
   "file": "vo/L79.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Five. Measure your work space. And keep your rent, utility, and internet bills."
  },
  {
   "id": "L80",
   "file": "vo/L80.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "So, what did we learn?"
  },
  {
   "id": "L81",
   "file": "vo/L81.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One. Your provincial tax follows where you live on December thirty-first."
  },
  {
   "id": "L82",
   "file": "vo/L82.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Two. Your payroll can use a different province. And the difference shows up on your return."
  },
  {
   "id": "L83",
   "file": "vo/L83.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Three. It can go either way: a bill or a refund."
  },
  {
   "id": "L84",
   "file": "vo/L84.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Four. A home office can cut the bill, but only with the detailed method and a T twenty-two hundred."
  },
  {
   "id": "L85",
   "file": "vo/L85.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Next on this channel: what happens to your taxes when you support your parents. Subscribe, so you don't miss it."
  }
 ],
